The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
owner = rq->hw_context->engine;
list_move(&rq->sched.link, pl);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when a request is preempted and returned to its original virtual engine, it can still complete in the background while being linked to the original physical engine. This can lead to the request being retired before the breadcrumb link is properly decoupled, causing inconsistencies in the request's lifecycle management.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (test_bit(DMA_FENCE_FLAG_ENABLE_SIGNAL_BIT, &rq->fence.flags)) {
    spin_lock(&rq->lock);
    i915_request_cancel_breadcrumb(rq);
    spin_unlock(&rq->lock);
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that before moving the request back to the virtual engine, the breadcrumb is decoupled by canceling it. This prevents the request from completing in the background while still linked to the original physical engine, thus maintaining the integrity of the request's lifecycle and avoiding potential inconsistencies.

